  Hello everyone,

  Today I tried to compile 2.6.0-test7. Aside some modules (which I don't have
hardware for anyway) the kernel compiled OK. Had to overcome some obstacles as
far as modules installation
(http://www.codemonkey.org.uk/post-halloween-2.5.txt). Only thing that bothered
is isp_mod is missing, I couldn't find an option for it in .config (make
menuconfig). Has it been merged with qlogicisp?
  Right now I still cannot boot new kernel due to some issues with ramdisk -
seems like mkinitrd didn't creat proper image, I mounted it on loopback and saw
only two files there: /bin/insmod and /bin/nash. Comparing to the 2.4.18-27.7
one that I have from distro, it's nothing. And the error I'm getting is:
VFS: Cannot open root device sda1....

  That happenes with almost everything I pass to root= option, including the
major/minor number for sda1, ram0, ram1, /dev/rd/0.

   I wonder if anyone had a better luck with this. I can send my .config file
if needed.

  Thanks,


