If you're compiling your own kernel, you might as well just link 
your boot-time drivers statically and dispense with a ramdisk. 
;-)

AFAIK the new 2.6 style of initrd is changed, btw, but I haven't 
checked into exactly what's different.  Something called 
initramfs IIRC.  I suspect it takes some new fancy dancing to 
build an initrd under 2.6, which would explain your initrd 
troubles.

