On Mon, 20 Oct 2003, Christos Papachristou wrote:

>1. Are there any plans in supporting the machine in future
>releases of the alpha linux port?

There are at the current time, no official Red Hat plans to
produce or support another Alpha distribution port in the future.

That said however, myself, Jeff Garzik, Richard Henderson, a few 
people from DEC/Compaq/HP, Phil Copeland, and others are 
interested in doing a volunteer developed port of current bits to 
Alpha.  We'd like to do this as part of the Fedora Project 
http://fedora.redhat.com if possible, or alternatively as a 
port/clone to Alpha.  There is no timeline or schedule for this 
planned as of yet however, and nothing has been started 
officially yet.


>2. I have read that this machine hase a MIPS emulation mode.
>Does this mean that it can be used with the MIPS linux port ,as
>if it were a DECstation?

Alpha and MIPS are very different architectures.  I've never 
heard of an Alpha that could emulate MIPS.


-- 
