On Mon, 20 Oct 2003, Christos Papachristou wrote:

> Two questions concerning the DEC3000/300LX:
>  
> 1. Are there any plans in supporting the machine in future releases of
> the alpha linux port? 

 I'm going to support the DEC 3000 line of systems as a part of our
TURBOchannel support as soon as I get appropriate hardware (the other
candidate for support being the VAXstation 4000/60, /90, etc.). 

> 2. I have read that this machine hase a MIPS emulation mode. Does this
> mean that it can be used with the MIPS linux port ,as if it were a
> DECstation? 

 The console code of DEC 3000 systems is capable of emulating MIPS I code
for the purpose of REX (aka TURBOchannel firmware) compatibility,
specifically for being able to execute option ROM code.  And that's all --
you can't run a MIPS OS on the systems using the emulator.  Besides,
hardware is different enough MIPS/Linux wouldn't work -- the emulator only
warrants appropriate emulating of I/O accesses for the slot an option ROM
is executing from plus calling the REX standard entry points from the so
called callback vector.

 Anyway, the DEC 3000 is fully specified and the onboard logic is similar
enough to one of the newer DECstations a port shouldn't be that difficult.

 Maciej

