These are details you worry about once you have seen for the
first time "bash-2.05a# ", or similar, prompt.

OTOH if you have machines for which "full-blown" desktop in a style
of current Linux distributions is too heavy but you still would
like to run a graphics environment then there are options.
CDE is out for multiple reasons but visit
http://www.xfce.org/
for example. CDE users will feel at home. There are other possibilities.

Oh, and Gnome with a reasonable window manager is not that heavy
after all.  Most likely you see this thingy called Nautilus
(an application which runs from gnome-session) which indeed can
eat any amount of resources.  Nothing really is forcing you to
run that.

   Michal

