On Mon, 20 Oct 2003, Donsbach, Jeff wrote:

> Indeed. And even before worrying about Window manager or desktop
> environment, the hard part is going to be coming up with XFree86 drivers
> that support those old Turbochannel graphics cards. Have the BSD ports
> done anything to get past this issue? 

 A number of graphics cards are already supported for the DECstation, so
they'll work for the Alpha after minor tweaking.  Unfortunately, they are
supported as dumb frame buffers only at the moment.  However, I'm
currently working on supporting ZLX-E series boards with the TGA driver
(the ASIC used on the boards is essentially the TGA with no PCI glue) --
the kernel driver is already working for me (the console is working as is
the dumb frame buffer DDX) and I suppose the TGA DDX should work after
minor tweaking.

