On Wed, 2003-10-22 at 17:11, George France wrote:
> That series of alpha returns a negative id number.  This used to identify NT 
> only systems.  In 2.4.x there is a couple of lines in 
> arch/alpha/kernel/setup.c in get_sysname, that changes the id from negative 
> to positive.  It was something that Jay Estabrook fixed a long long time ago.  
> Anyway the 2 lines of code fell out of 2.6.x, for some reason.

I found the two lines you are talking about:

	if (type < 0)
	type = -type;

I added them to setup.c in the same function.  Recompiled and tried to
boot.  Same instant reboot.

But I see through out setup.c compairing 2.4.19 to 2.6.0-test8 that a
lot of the variable types have been cleaned up.  "type" is now an
"unsigned long".  Where in 2.4 it was just a "long".

That is probably why the lines were removed, but how should this be
fixed now?

-- 
Chris



