I initially joined linux-alpha, and posted a few patches to get a mid
2.5 kernel to build on the Alpha.  I was told then that the list was
pretty much dead, and to retry on axp-list.

Indeed, linux-alpha is a very dead list, no kernel development going on
there, just an occasional post asking if the list is still alive.

I don't run Redhat on my Alpha, but I also don't run Debian, Gentoo, or
any distro for that matter, just my own custom install (boot strapped
with an old Slackware for Alpha actually).

I'm still on linux-alpha, and I plan to stay on axp-list also.  I'm just
where the people are.  I don't need help too often, and don't have much
to offer in most cases, having only owned one Alpha.  But interesting
discussions do occur here from time to time, this is a really great
group of people, and I'm happy to be part of it.

-- 
Chris



