While scanning through the GNU mailman options for axp-list, I 
just noticed that monthly password reminder emailings was 
disabled.  Since there were a rather large number of people 
recently who asked to be unsubscribed from the list once mgalgoci 
posted about the list changes, I figured it would be a good idea 
to enable this option, as most if not all other redhat.com 
mailing lists have this enabled.

So, from now on, everyone on this list will receive a single 
email message at the end of the month which gives you your list 
password, and instructions on how to unsubscribe/change options, 
etc.  This should make it a bit easier for people to unsubscribe 
who forget how and don't have the time to try to figure it out.

As always, to unsubscribe from this list, you can visit the GNU 
mailman webpages located at:

	https://www.redhat.com/mailman/listinfo/axp-list

Follow the instructions on the above web page, and type in your
password in the proper text box and submit to unsubscribe.  If 
you don't remember your password, there is a place you can click 
to have your password emailed out to you.  Once you receive the 
password via email, you can go back to the web page above and 
unsubscribe, or change list options, etc.

Take care,
TTYL


-- 
Mike A. Harris     ftp://people.redhat.com/mharris
OS Systems Engineer - XFree86 maintainer - Red Hat



