On Mon, Oct 27, 2003 at 12:00:49AM -0500, Arkadiy Chapkis - Arc wrote:
> Oct 26 23:05:24 baltika kernel: module snd_page_alloc: Relocation overflow vs
> section 20

I've seen that too.

>   My guess is that the first line is the culprit - because snd_page_alloc
> doesn't load, everything else is not loading either.

Exactly.

>   My question is: should I file kernel bug report, or is it something I do
> wrong?

I think there is a problem with incorrect sign extension in calculation
of GPRELHIGH value in alpha/kernel/module.c. The appended patch works
for me, though I'm not sure it's right way to fix that - I've sent this
to rth 3 or 4 times, but it wasn't applied...

Ivan.

--- 2.6/arch/alpha/kernel/module.c	Wed May 28 01:05:20 2003
+++ linux/arch/alpha/kernel/module.c	Mon Aug 11 23:23:02 2003
@@ -259,7 +259,7 @@ apply_relocate_add(Elf64_Shdr *sechdrs, 
 			*(u64 *)location = value;
 			break;
 		case R_ALPHA_GPRELHIGH:
-			value = (value - gp + 0x8000) >> 16;
+			value = (long)(value - gp + 0x8000) >> 16;
 			if ((short) value != value)
 				goto reloc_overflow;
 			*(u16 *)location = value;



