> Well, the new DS15 uses ev6x CPU technology and now to be considered
> ancient memory technology. I'm pretty sure that it is based on the last
> incarnation of the "Tsunami" Chipset the world will ever see (and which
> was originally introduced back in 1999). A new single-CPU ev7-based
> workstation surely would have deserved more attention that this box.

DS15 CPU is indeed EV68, I think around 1GHz.

DS15 core logic is TITAN, successor to TSUNAMI, and used in DS25/ES45.

DS15 is intended as replacement/upgrade from DS10, necessitated primarily
because of EOL on TSUNAMI chipset by INTEL.

