On Mon, Oct 27, 2003 at 06:59:47PM +0100, Stefan Schroepfer wrote:
> Jay Estabrook wrote:
> > 
> > DS15 core logic is TITAN, successor to TSUNAMI, and used in DS25/ES45.
> > 
> > DS15 is intended as replacement/upgrade from DS10, necessitated primarily
> > because of EOL on TSUNAMI chipset by INTEL.
> 
> Thanks for the info. On first sight, I overlooked this difference, as
> the block digrams of DS10 and DS15 are very similar, consisting of one
> C-Chip, two D-Chips and one P-Chip in each case. My fault.

Easy to do.

And actually, TITAN P-Chip (aka PA-chip) supports 2 PCI buses (or 1
PCI and 1 AGP), so the builtin devices (NIC/etc) are on 1 PCI bus, and
the riser PCI slots are on the other; note also that two of the PCI
slots are capable of 66MHz speed, and NONE of the slots support 5V
cards.

