  OK, I finally got sound to work. Unfortunately I had to go back to OSS
modules, as neither one of ALSA worked for me. Unfortunately, because it seems
that OSS will be going away and the best I could get with ALSA
snd_sb8 is some hissing sound while playing with aplay. Not to mention that
/dev/snd/pcmC0D0* weren't available (I made the with MAKDEV.snd, but couldn't
redirect a sound file to those). I tried every dma setting and had to use
alsamixer to upped the channels every time I loaded modules.

  I am still very gratefull to Ivan for his patch (who knows, maybe OSS
wouldn't load as well if not for this patch and I wouldn't be able to listen to
M. Magomaev right now). Also I'd like to thank Jay for his pointers (I may
still need them in future).

>
>I think there is a problem with incorrect sign extension in calculation
>of GPRELHIGH value in alpha/kernel/module.c. The appended patch works
>for me, though I'm not sure it's right way to fix that - I've sent this
>to rth 3 or 4 times, but it wasn't applied...
>
>Ivan.
>
>--- 2.6/arch/alpha/kernel/module.c	Wed May 28 01:05:20 2003
>+++ linux/arch/alpha/kernel/module.c	Mon Aug 11 23:23:02 2003
>@@ -259,7 +259,7 @@ apply_relocate_add(Elf64_Shdr *sechdrs, 
> 			*(u64 *)location = value;
> 			break;
> 		case R_ALPHA_GPRELHIGH:
>-			value = (value - gp + 0x8000) >> 16;
>+			value = (long)(value - gp + 0x8000) >> 16;
> 			if ((short) value != value)
> 				goto reloc_overflow;
> 			*(u16 *)location = value;
>
>


                                      Arc C.
                                      achapkis@dls.net



