Just a friendly notice to everyone that about a week or so ago,
when the mailing list was restored and some administrative
cleanups of dead accounts were done, that there were many more
accounts that were unknowns.  Mailman's bounce detection was
enabled and set to auto-unsubscribe mail accounts resulting in 
bouncing.

Since mailman is quite conservative with this option, it tries to
err on the side of caution, and does not disable subscriptions 
right away.  It takes a short while for it to hit a bounce 
threshhold at which time it determines the account must be dead 
or otherwise problematic, then it unsubscribes the bouncing 
accounts.

Today, bounce detection kicked in, and unsubscribed about 20-30 
subcriptions to the list automatically.  Just to make sure that 
this was not a goofup, I decided to post this message here to 
inform people that the unsubscribes were automated via mailman's 
bounce detection.

As such, if anyone was inadvertently unsubscribed or knows 
someone who happened to get unsubscribed, please just resubscribe 
manually and everything should be ok.  As always, make sure your 
email accounts don't run out of disk quota, etc. as that causes 
mail bounces, and if enough collect up, mailman will auto 
unsubscribe people.

Thanks,
TTYL


