I was happily running 7.1 on my XL366 (AlphaBIOS, milo) and I decided in
a rash moment to upgrade to 7.2
I then load milo and...  boot scd0:/kernels/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/scd0
initrd=images/cdrom.img   ...chugs away.

It suggested I alter my filesystems to EXT3 - urm.. Ok, fair enough.
At the end of the upgrade it tells me it doesn't support Milo.
Urm.. Oh.. Well, it didn't matter before, so what the hey.

I'm using boot sda1:vmlinux-2.4.9-32.5 root=/dev/sda9  which is the same
as I used for 7.1 but with the new kernel. 
Just change the version number in the AlphaBIOS entry so that it matches
the result from    milo ls sda1:
Alas, after the upgrade I can no longer boot - it complains that it
can't mount the root filesystem.

Soo.. I decided to Install rather than Upgrade and reformatted both
sda1: /boot and also sda9: / as EXT2 in case that was the problem.
Let it chug away and.. No go.

Still boots NT4 ok, so it's not the hardware - clearly this is
user-error :-]
It's a long time since I last wrestled with this.. Have I
forgotten/overlooked something?

Waah! I need the Alpha back up so I can play with the VAX port.
Luke 



