> 
>   I looked very briefly at it on the compaq ftp site and didn't 
>   really understand what it was for.
>   I got the impression it was for other models - I shall revisit !

Yes, it WAS intended specifically to help on models NOT supported by
the earlier (original) release (ie MARVEL, 2100A, and DAC960-based
machines).

However, it does have a bit more "infrastructure" and post-install
help for MILO-based machines.

But it's not worth using if you've already done the install with the
original, as it only provides updated RPMS (beyond the 7.2 originals)
in a few special cases that were needed for post-install support on
those specific machines mentioned above.

Good luck.

